# End-to-end QEMU coverage of spec-crash-capture AC-3 and assumptions A-2, A-3, A-5: a kernel panic on an
# appliance that reserves a crash region is harvested by the next boot into /perm/ze/crash.
#
# Drives internal/le/test/qemu/crashcapture.go, which builds a HOST ze, inits an
# appliance whose config carries image.crash-dump, seeds `set system crash-dump enabled true`
# and kernel.unknown_nmi_panic, boots the image in QEMU, waits for `show crashes | json`
# to report the region armed, injects an NMI through the QEMU monitor, and asserts the
# next boot lists a kernel-kind artifact whose text carries the panic line.
#
# amd64 only. The driver self-skips with a clear reason on another architecture, or
# when QEMU, sshpass, e2fsprogs, or the go toolchain are absent. It exits 0 in both
# PASS and SKIP cases; a genuine failure exits non-zero, as does an appliance that
# never answers under a hardware accelerator.
#
# The explicit timeout covers a host ze build, an appliance init, a full gokrazy image
# build and two QEMU boots; vpp-hugepages-qemu.ci explains why it is pinned.
option=timeout:value=900s
cmd=foreground:seq=1:exec=./le test qemu crash-capture-panic-harvest
expect=exit:code=0
expect=stdout:pattern=APPLIANCE-CRASH-CAPTURE-QEMU: (PASS|SKIP)
